# {{ s.name }} — Unity Scene Transition

**Variant:** `{{ variant }}`
**Load mode:** `{{ s.load_mode }}`
**Trigger:** `{{ s.trigger }}`
**Target scene:** `{{ s.target_scene }}`

{{ s.description }}

## Install

1. Drop the `Scripts/` folder into your project's `Assets/`.
2. Add **{{ s.target_scene }}** (and this scene) to **Build Settings → Scenes In Build**.
3. Add the `{{ s.name }}` component to a GameObject.
{% if variant in ("fade", "trigger_door") %}
4. Create a full-screen black `Image` with a `CanvasGroup` (alpha 0) and assign it to `fadeCanvas`.
{% endif %}
{% if variant == "loading_bar" %}
4. Add a `Slider` and assign it to `progressBar` (fills as the scene streams in).
{% endif %}
{% if s.trigger == "on_trigger" %}
5. Put this object's collider on **Is Trigger** and tag your player `{{ s.player_tag }}`.
{% elif s.trigger == "on_timer" %}
5. Fires automatically {{ "%.0f"|format(s.timer_delay) }}s after the scene starts.
{% else %}
5. Call `Go()` from your code/UI when you want the transition to run.
{% endif %}

## Behaviour

{% if variant == "instant" %}
Loads `{{ s.target_scene }}` immediately ({{ s.load_mode }}).
{% elif variant in ("fade", "trigger_door") %}
Fades to black over {{ "%.1f"|format(s.fade_duration) }}s, then loads `{{ s.target_scene }}` ({{ s.load_mode }}).
{% elif variant == "loading_bar" %}
Streams `{{ s.target_scene }}` asynchronously while updating the progress bar (0–1).
{% elif variant == "async_additive" %}
Loads `{{ s.target_scene }}` additively in the background (keeps the current scene live).
{% endif %}
`Go()` is public and idempotent (guards against double-trigger).
